{
 "name": "NorthLedger context terms: the only words a web search for the AI report may use",
 "version": "2026-09-30.1",
 "about": [
  "The AI-written report may cite public sources found by web searches. A search is never written by the AI or taken from the visitor's file: the planner picks terms from the lists below, and the adapter (engine/nl_browser.py _context_queries) builds each search from those terms and years only. A term that is not on its list, exactly as normalised below, drops the whole search.",
  "Generic terms only: macroeconomic and market indicators, industries (never a brand, a company or a product name), and places (world regions, countries and territories by their English short names, Canada's provinces and territories, the US states and the District of Columbia, and 50 major cities). Every term is ASCII and holds no digit.",
  "A term that happens to equal a value in the visitor's file (a region column that holds Ontario) is still a list term: the search holds the list's own spelling of it, and nothing else from the file.",
  "Georgia is one entry for the country and the US state (region_groups counts it with the countries).",
  "Kept in step: the worker's planner prompt and plan check (insight-proxy) copy this file; tools/pack_engine.py packs it beside the adapter in the browser engine; profile_for_ai sends its version (context_terms_version) so the planner can tell which list the adapter reads."
 ],
 "normalise": "NFKD, combining marks (accents) removed, case-folded, every run of characters that are not letters or digits read as one space, trimmed. 'Cote d'Ivoire', 'C\u00f4te d'Ivoire' and 'cote d ivoire' are the same term; 'ecommerce' is not 'e-commerce'.",
 "compose": "One search per item: [sector] indicator [region] [from year] [to year, when it differs], each term in this file's own spelling, joined by single spaces. Examples: 'consumer price inflation Canada 2024 2025', 'video games sales growth 2023'.",
 "plan_field": {
  "name": "context",
  "max_items": 4,
  "item": {
   "indicator": "required: a term from indicators",
   "sector": "optional: a term from sectors (absent, null or an empty string: none)",
   "region": "optional: a term from regions (absent, null or an empty string: none)",
   "years": "optional: [from, to] or [year]: integers (a 4-digit string is read as its integer), each 1900 to 2099, from not after to"
  },
  "rules": "An item with any term not on its list, or years out of range, is dropped whole. Other keys in an item are ignored. After 4 searches, or a search already built, the rest are dropped. The plan's old free-text context_queries is never read."
 },
